# The real config lives outside the webroot and never enters git.
#
# ONLY the repo-root one. The leading slash is load-bearing: a bare `config.php`
# matches at ANY depth, which silently excluded lib/config.php — a core source file
# every script requires — from the initial commit until 13 Sep 2026. A fresh clone
# fatally failed on every entrypoint and nothing said why, because an ignored file
# does not show up in git status.
#
# The deploy layout's real config lives at ../config.php, outside the repo entirely,
# so no rule here is what protects it.
/config.php

# Local dev overrides
.env
*.local.php

# Logs and scratch output
logs/
*.log
/tmp/
/var/

# Verification output written by bin/verify-endpoints.php.
# The generated report IS committed: it is 17 real calls with timings and outcomes, and
# it is the evidence behind docs/api-friction.md. It contains no key — the verifier
# redacts, and CMC does not echo the header back.
# The live payloads are not: they are large, they go stale, and they are one command to
# regenerate. tests/live_test.php skips cleanly when they are absent.
# Note the trailing /* : git does not descend into an excluded *directory*, so
# "tests/fixtures/live/" would make the negation below silently do nothing.
tests/fixtures/live/*
!tests/fixtures/live/README.md

# OS noise
.DS_Store
._*
Thumbs.db

# Editors
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
